# Citation metadata for OncoTriage Agent, in Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# GitHub parses this file and renders the "Cite this repository" control from
# it; a file that fails schema validation renders nothing at all and says
# nothing about why, so validate after editing:
#
#     pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate -i CITATION.cff
#
# THE LICENCE IS NAMED HERE, AND IT USED TO BE UNNAMEABLE. `license:` takes an
# SPDX identifier and only an SPDX identifier, and this project's former terms
# were a bespoke all-rights-reserved text with no identifier on the SPDX License
# List -- so the key was omitted and `license-url` carried a link instead, which
# is the field the schema provides for exactly that case ("only for non-standard
# licenses not included in the SPDX License List"). The project is now under
# PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0, whose identifier IS on the SPDX License List and
# IS in the CFF 1.2.0 enum, so `license:` carries it and `license-url` is gone:
# keeping a non-standard-licence field beside a standard identifier would assert
# the opposite of what is true. LICENSE remains the authority; this is a label.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, so nobody adds it back by guessing: there is no
# `doi:` and no `preferred-citation:` because no DOI has been minted and no
# paper exists; no `date-released:` because this version carries no release tag
# to date; and no author `orcid:` because no tracked file in this repository
# records one, and a citation file is not the place to invent one. The author
# `email:` IS recorded, deliberately: PolyForm Noncommercial permits
# noncommercial use without asking, and permits commercial use not at all, so a
# commercial licence has to be negotiated and that request needs an address to
# go to.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: OncoTriage Agent
message: >-
  If you reference this software, please cite it as below. Reuse is permitted
  for noncommercial purposes under the terms in LICENSE (PolyForm Noncommercial
  1.0.0); commercial use requires a separate licence from the copyright holder.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alsaffar
    given-names: Ramy
    email: ramyalsaffar@gmail.com
version: "2.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ramyalsaffar/OncoTriage-Agent"
abstract: >-
  OncoTriage Agent matches oncology patients, represented as Synthea FHIR
  bundles, to recruiting ClinicalTrials.gov trials. It runs a six-stage
  LangGraph pipeline over hybrid BM25 and dense-vector retrieval on Qdrant,
  with a large language model performing criterion-level eligibility
  evaluation. It is a research and engineering demonstration on synthetic
  patient data and is not for clinical use.
keywords:
  - clinical trials
  - oncology
  - patient matching
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - LangGraph
  - FHIR
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
